  "rationale": "The plant models robot motion and perception as open-loop pulses and sensor events. The specification enforces conservative exploration: random_walk in clear, move_forward only after random_walk, and immediate turn-based recovery on obstacles. Each obstacle triggers a dedicated recovery state with a single turn action, and only path_clear allows return to exploration. No forward or random_walk is enabled in obstacle states, and no oscillation or deadlock is possible.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant for motion/perception and specification for safe exploration policy",
    "Use helper commit/recovery states to enforce one-shot actions and conservative obstacle handling"
  ],
